flowchart TB
  accTitle: How the packages of Gemini and Copilot reach the job analyze
  accDescr: Renovate updates the lock file of the Gemini CLI or the Copilot CLI in engines/, the command line a week after its release and the other packages every Monday, each package at one version with its SHA-512 hash. The check engine contracts of the pull request installs the lock file as analyze does, verifies the signature of npm's registry of every package and the attestations of those that have them, and makes sure that npm refuses another hash; a failure keeps the update from merging. A patch version merges on its own once every required check passed, a minor or major version and the refresh of the other packages when the maintainer merges them, and a release brings it to every repository. In the job analyze, the checkout of the issue assistant at the commit of the workflow holds the lock file, and npm ci installs it in a folder of the run, without the scripts of the packages and without the engine's secret, from npm's registry alone. A package whose hash isn't the one of the lock file stops the analysis before anything of it runs; otherwise the command line runs with the engine's secret.
  renovate["`**Renovate** updates engines/gemini/ or engines/copilot/:<br>the command line a week after its release,<br>the other packages every Monday`"]
  check["`**The check engine contracts**<br>installs the lock file as analyze does,<br>verifies every signature and attestation,<br>and npm must refuse another hash`"]
  merge["`**A patch version merges on its own,**<br>a minor or major one and the refresh<br>when the maintainer merges them;<br>a release brings it to every repository`"]
  analyze["`**The job analyze**: npm ci of the lock file<br>at the commit of the workflow, no scripts,<br>no secret for npm, npm's registry alone`"]
  runs(["The command line runs with the engine's secret"])
  waits(["The update doesn't merge"])
  stops(["The analysis stops before anything of the package runs"])
  renovate --> check
  check -- "green" --> merge --> analyze
  analyze -- "every hash is the one of the lock file" --> runs
  check -. "a signature fails,<br>or npm takes another hash" .-> waits
  analyze -. "another hash" .-> stops
  classDef trigger fill:#d4a72c33,stroke:#bf8700,stroke-width:2px
  classDef job fill:#8c959f1f,stroke:#8c959f,stroke-width:2px
  classDef safe fill:#1a7f3726,stroke:#1a7f37,stroke-width:2px
  classDef stop fill:#cf222e26,stroke:#cf222e,stroke-width:2px
  class renovate trigger
  class check,merge,analyze job
  class runs safe
  class waits,stops stop
